    "snippet": "---\ntitle: 17 Actors and Their First On Screen Appearances\nauthor: Megan Diane\ndate: 2021-09-29\n---\nHere are 17 actors and their first on screen appearances in movies and television.\n\nEvery actor has to start somewhere. Many A-list actors also had humble beginnings with small roles, one-liners, and even background extra roles. Here are several A-list actors and their first on-screen appearances.\n\n1. Robert Downey Jr.\n\nRobert Downey Jr., 5 y old, making his screen debut in the movie \"Pound\" released in 1970, written and directed by his father Robert Downey Sr. His only line is: \"Have any hair on your balls?\"\n\nSource:  \n\n2. Leonardo DiCaprio\n\nLeonardo DiCaprio, age 9, auditioning for \"The Outsiders\" (1983). Unfortunately, he didn't get the part. Instead, his career began with his appearance in several commercials, educational films and as a supporting cast member of the sitcom \"Growing Pains\" (1985). It wasn't until 1989 that DiCaprio landed his first credited role: two episodes of \"The New Lassie\".\n\nSource:  \n\n3. Anthony Hopkins\n\nAnthony Hopkins made his first professional stage appearance in the Palace Theatre, Swansea, in 1960 with Swansea Little Theatre's production of \"Have a Cigarette\". In 1965 (age 28) he made his screen debut as Dr. Harding on the TV series \"The Man in Room 17\".\n\nSource:  \n\n4. Angelina Jolie\n\nAs the daughter of actor Jon Voight, Angelina Jolie appeared in the media from an early age. Her she is, 7 years of age, in her first feature film \"Lookin' To Get Out\" (1982) as Tosh\u2026 Also starring her father.\n\nSource:  \n\n5. Reese Witherspoon\n\nIn 1991, Reese Witherspoon (age 15) attended an open casting call for \"The Man in the Moon\", intending to audition as a bit player, she was instead cast for the lead role of Dani Trant, a 14-year-old country girl who falls in love for the first time with her 17-year-old neighbor. Her performance was regarded as \"memorably touching\" by Variety magazine, and critic Roger Ebert commented, \"Her first kiss is one of the most perfect little scenes I've ever seen in a movie.\n\nSource: \n\n"
